{
  "stem": "advanced_shipping_2023_W41_ADVANCED-MARKET-REPORT-WEEK-41",
  "source_file": "advanced_shipping_2023_W41_ADVANCED-MARKET-REPORT-WEEK-41.pdf",
  "issue_date": "2023-10-13",
  "report_week": "41",
  "report_period": "Week 41 (6th Oct to 13th Oct 2023)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Diana Shipping have sold their Capesize \"Boston\" 177/2007 SWS, China (SS 06/2027, DD 07/2025) to Greek buyers for USD 18 mill. Remind you that back in July, the \"Aquakatie\"174/2007 SWS, China (SS/DD 02/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 15,9 mill. The Panamax \"HC Pioneer\" 75/2004 Sanoyas, Japan (SS/DD 05/2024) of Dongguan Haichang Industrial was committed to Chinese buyers for high USD 8 mill. For reference, the sister vessel \"Navios Anthos\" 75/2004 Sanoyas, Japan (SS/DD 09/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold back in April at USD 11,25 mill. Parakou Shipping have sold their Ultramax \"CP Shanghai\" 63/2015 Chengxi, China (SS/DD 08/2025, BWTS fitted) for region USD 23,5 mill. Note that back in July, the \"Kambos\" 63/2015 Cosco, China (SS/DD 06/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 24,5 mill. On the Supramax sector, RHL Reederei have sold their \"RHL Clarita\" 53/2008 Chengxi, China (SS 03/2028, DD 05/2025, BWTS fitted) at USD 9,5 mill, while the one-year-older sister vessel \"RHL Marta\" 53/2007 Chengxi, China (SS 10/2027, DD 01/2026, BWTS fitted) was sold in July at mid USD 10 mill. Furthermore, the \"Star Zeta\" 53/2003 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 11/2023) was committed to Hong Kong based buyers at USD 8 mill. Note that a month ago, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Jin Feng\" 52/2004 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 12/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 8,1 mill. Following the sale of the Handysize \"Purple Sea\" 35/2011 Nantong, China (SS 06/2026, DD 06/2024, BWTS fitted) a couple of weeks ago at USD 10,9 mill, Purple Sea Holding have now committed the sister vessel \"Red Sea\" 35/2011 Nantong, China (SS 08/2026, DD 11/2024, BWTS fitted) for USD 11 mill. Moreover, the \"Leni Selmer\" 35/2011 Samjin, China (SS 11/2026, DD 01/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold to Greek buyers Roxette for USD 11,55 mill.",
    "tankers": "Chemikalien Seetransport have committed their LR1 \"Chemtrans Aegean\" 76/2007 Dalian, China (SS 08/2027, DD 11/2025, BWTS fitted) to undisclosed buyers for USD 22 mill. For reference, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Hafnia Rhine\" 76/2008 Dalian, China (SS 03/2028, DD 03/2026, BWTS fitted) was sold back in April at USD 26,5 mill. Dong-A Tanker have committed on subs their MR2 \"Dong-A Themis\" 50/2015 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS/DD 01/2025, BWTS fitted) for USD 38 mill, while the one-year-younger \"Lacerta\" & \"Bora Bora\" 50/2016 Spp, Korea (SS 06/2026, DD 06/2024 & SS 03/2026, DD 07/2024 respectively, BWTS fitted) of TMS tankers were committed to Turkish buyers for USD 40,5 mill each.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of high usd 10,00's low usd 11,00's fio range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 13,000/16,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed at the usd 12,000/14,000 pd range. Indonesian trips into Philippines were fixed around usd 13,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 150K. A number of Indonesian trips into India were reported at the level of usd 16,000 pd. South East Asian trips via East Coast South America into China were fixed around usd 14,000/16,000 pd. Indian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 16,000/18,000 pd. Indian Coastal trips were fixed around usd 12,000/13,000 pd. South African trips into India were reported at the level of usd 14,250 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 425K. Inter-Continental trips via West Africa were fixed around usd 16,000/18,000 pd. Continental trips via US East Coast into India were reported at the level of usd 25,000/27,000 pd. US Gulf trips into China were fixed around usd 19,500 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 950K. South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 16,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 600K. A Kamsarmax was fixed on period at the usd 16,000 pd basis delivery China for 4/6 months employment.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of Indonesian trips into India were fixed around usd 12,000/14,000 pd. A number of Australian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 12,000/14,000 pd. East Coast Indian trips via South Africa into West Coast India were fixed around usd 13,000/15,000 pd. South African trips into China were reported at the level of usd 23,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 240K. US Gulf trips into Continent were fixed around usd 14,000/15,000 pd. US Gulf trips into East Coast Central America were reported at the level of usd 15,000/16,000 pd. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "A number of Persian Gulf trips into East Coast India were reported at the level of usd 8,000/9,000 pd. West African trips via Continent into US Gulf were fixed around usd 13,000/14,000 pd. Caribbean trips via East Coast South America into West Coast Central America were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
